WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.917
On this slide, we are focusing on choose the right visual.

00:00:03.917 --> 00:00:08.532
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.532 --> 00:00:17.337
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:17.337 --> 00:00:23.192
Choose the visual based on the question: bars for categories, lines for time, histograms for distributions,

00:00:23.192 --> 00:00:25.617
and scatter plots for relationships.

00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:28.587
Separate calculation from interpretation.

00:00:28.587 --> 00:00:36.162
A statistic summarizes the sample and a visualization reveals pattern, but both still require context,

00:00:36.162 --> 00:00:39.367
variability, and awareness of limitations.

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:45.127
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:45.127 --> 00:00:50.546
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
